The KNN algorithm involves the following steps:-

1)Calculate Distances:-
      Compute the distance between the test data point and all other data points in the training set.
      Select the number of nearest neighbors, K (e.g., K = 3 or K = 5), which acts as a hyperparameter for the model.
2)Sort Distances:-
      Sort the distances in ascending order.
      Compute the distance between the target test data point and all other data points in the training set using a distance metric like Euclidean, Manhattan, or Minkowski distance
3)Select Neighbors:-
      Choose the k nearest neighbors based on the sorted distances.
      Rank all calculated distances in ascending order and select the top K points with the shortest distance to the test sample
4)Vote or Average:-
    • For Classification:
          Perform a majority vote among the K neighbors and assign the most frequent class label to the test point.
    • For Regression: 
          Calculate the mean (average) value of the target variable across the K neighbors to predict a continuous value
